0009: NV12 + MUTABLE loses UBWC, not the tiling.

**Status:** shipped in `27.0.0-devel-p14`. Upstream: an upstream candidate as a
separate `tu_image.cc` fix (it removes an unnecessary demotion and adds no chip
checks) - not sent yet.
**Found:** `tu_image.cc` gave NV12 + MUTABLE two restrictions at
once, and the second one made the combination uncreatable under 0004.

## For users of other drivers

Nothing to set. NV12 + MUTABLE stops being linear, and NV12 + MUTABLE + sparse
becomes creatable at all. On a stock driver without 0004 the image is still
creatable but linear.

## Summary

In the planar NV12 branch, images with `VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT` got
`ubwc_enabled = false` *and* `force_linear_tile = true`. The first is necessary
(the Y plane is compressed in a way that does not survive reinterpretation); the
second is redundant: the layout is built by the same format (`tu6_plane_format()`
returns `PIPE_FORMAT_Y8_UNORM` for plane 0), so only the compression differs. A
linear sparse image cannot be addressed (0004), which is how the redundancy
turned into a refusal.

## Evidence

One hunk in `tu_image.cc`. Verified by probe `N` of
`tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test.c`: stock SUCCESS, 0004-0008
`FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT`, plus this patch SUCCESS - and the 0004 gate refuses
exactly when `tile_mode != TILE6_3`, so SUCCESS means tiled directly. Planar
layouts: probe `W`, journal 18.

## Tests

| what the hunk changes | how it is checked | result |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| NV12+MUTABLE+SPARSE is creatable | probe `N`, journal 18 | `FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT -> SUCCESS` |
| the layout is still the same plane | probe `W` planar layouts, journal 18 | unchanged |
| nothing else moves | the 94-row matrix, journal 24.3 | 94 EXACT |

## The change in this repo

It may drop the tiling ban, never the UBWC ban; it must not move any other format
between tiled and linear. Revert: `git apply -R` with the file name explicit.

## Related

`0004` (the refusal this removes the vkd3d path into); ADR-0003.

